WEBVTT

00:01.213 --> 00:04.909
<i>It seems today that all you see</i>

00:04.945 --> 00:08.182
<i>Is violence in movies and sex on TV</i>

00:08.218 --> 00:11.821
<i>But where are those
good old-fashioned values</i>

00:11.855 --> 00:14.824
<i>On which we used to rely?</i>

00:14.858 --> 00:18.327
<i>Lucky there's a family guy</i>

00:18.362 --> 00:21.697
<i>Lucky there's a man
who positively can do</i>

00:21.732 --> 00:23.266
<i>All the things that make us</i>

00:23.300 --> 00:24.667
<i>Laugh and cry</i>

00:24.701 --> 00:30.239
<i>He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy!</i>

00:43.053 --> 00:44.921
At last, I shall exact my vengeance

00:44.955 --> 00:46.522
and snuff out the miserable flame

00:46.556 --> 00:49.025
that has been your life, vile woman.

00:49.059 --> 00:51.694
<i>Growing one carrot</i>

00:51.728 --> 00:54.530
<i>Taking up time</i>

00:54.564 --> 00:58.868
<i>Filling up the day with nonsense</i>

00:58.902 --> 01:02.371
<i>Vodka in the bushes</i>

01:06.076 --> 01:09.879
<i>Making it better, making it bright</i>

01:09.913 --> 01:11.647
<i>What a day</i>

01:11.682 --> 01:13.916
<i>Think I'll check the mail.</i>

01:13.951 --> 01:17.420
Time to put you out of your misery.

01:19.923 --> 01:21.390
What the deuce?

01:21.425 --> 01:22.892
Sorry I broke your toy.

01:22.926 --> 01:25.161
Toy? This is a drone.

01:25.195 --> 01:27.763
Grown men who have never had
sexual relations

01:27.798 --> 01:29.098
fly them over people's houses

01:29.132 --> 01:30.733
to try and see something. I don't know.

01:30.767 --> 01:32.669
Here, want to play with my toy?

01:32.705 --> 01:34.904
- What the hell is this?
- It's a magic wand.

01:34.938 --> 01:36.639
Watch. Alakazam!

01:36.673 --> 01:38.240
I cast the tickle spell.

01:39.643 --> 01:40.910
Okay, okay, you got me.

01:40.944 --> 01:43.913
But seriously, cross me again,
and I will end you.

01:43.947 --> 01:46.082
You're funny. My name's Hudson.

01:46.116 --> 01:47.750
Want to play "spin in a circle"?

01:47.784 --> 01:49.919
I'm Stewie. Yeah, I don't think I...

01:49.953 --> 01:51.320
What the...? Stop it!

01:51.355 --> 01:53.122
I'm losing track of my surroundings.

01:53.156 --> 01:55.591
Hey, this is kind of fun.

01:55.625 --> 01:56.926
Whee!

01:56.960 --> 01:58.461
Yes. Whee.

01:58.495 --> 02:00.129
Whee!

02:01.498 --> 02:03.766
Oh, my. Oh, my.

02:03.800 --> 02:05.368
Hudson, time to go.

02:05.402 --> 02:06.769
I got to go home now.

02:06.803 --> 02:08.371
I'm glad I met you, Stewie.

02:08.405 --> 02:09.872
You're neat. Bye.

02:09.906 --> 02:11.340
Bye, Hudson.

02:11.375 --> 02:12.608
I like him.

02:12.642 --> 02:14.944
He's more fun than an Eddie Murphy bed.

02:14.978 --> 02:16.479
And check this out.

02:18.648 --> 02:20.616
That's cool. Is it a queen?

02:20.650 --> 02:24.320
Not sure, but people have said it is.

02:29.993 --> 02:32.228
Wait a minute.

02:32.262 --> 02:34.630
This is a self-empowerment seminar.

02:34.664 --> 02:35.731
You lied to me.

02:35.766 --> 02:37.566
You said we were going
to Baskin-Robbins.

02:37.601 --> 02:40.536
I said we were going
to bask in Robbins' glow.

02:40.570 --> 02:42.138
You know what you did.

02:42.172 --> 02:43.472
I do.

02:43.507 --> 02:45.975
Ladies and gentlemen,

02:46.009 --> 02:48.811
give it up for Tony Robbins.

02:57.387 --> 02:59.422
How the (BLEEP) is everyone?

02:59.456 --> 03:02.525
Ooh, he swore. I trust this guy.

03:02.561 --> 03:05.159
All of you here are capable
of greatness.

03:05.195 --> 03:06.662
Yay!

03:06.696 --> 03:08.531
But some will never achieve it.

03:08.565 --> 03:09.932
Oh, no!

03:09.966 --> 03:11.167
You, sir.

03:11.201 --> 03:13.035
Come out here.

03:17.040 --> 03:20.342
Sheesh, your head is the size
of a picnic watermelon.

03:20.377 --> 03:22.011
Ha! I've been told that.

03:22.045 --> 03:24.046
And you sound like you were lost at sea

03:24.081 --> 03:27.016
and told not to drink seawater
but drank seawater.

03:27.050 --> 03:29.051
Peter, will you just listen to him?

03:29.086 --> 03:30.853
Tony, this is why I brought him.

03:30.887 --> 03:33.856
He's never willing
to actually confront his issues.

03:33.890 --> 03:36.225
Sounds like you have no self-esteem.

03:36.259 --> 03:38.027
I don't deserve self-esteem.

03:38.061 --> 03:40.196
Peter, I was once a lot like you:

03:40.230 --> 03:43.899
unmotivated, dangerously obese,
always relying on cutaways...

03:43.934 --> 03:45.601
You know, that reminds me of the time...

03:45.635 --> 03:47.036
No, Peter. No more cutaways.

03:47.070 --> 03:48.704
- Stay in the present.
- Okay.

03:48.738 --> 03:51.040
Okay. Now tell me what you feel.

03:51.074 --> 03:53.042
Uh, a partial erection.

03:53.076 --> 03:54.910
I don't get touched very often.

03:54.945 --> 03:57.379
You know you deserve
a better life, right, Peter?

03:57.414 --> 03:59.748
Yes. Getting hard to breathe in here.

03:59.783 --> 04:01.784
I want to give you that life, Peter.

04:01.818 --> 04:04.386
Time to seize your personal power.

04:05.856 --> 04:07.756
Yeah, by getting away from you,
you weirdo.

04:07.791 --> 04:09.892
But first, here's that cutaway
I was gonna do

04:09.926 --> 04:11.160
before you made me skip it.

04:11.194 --> 04:13.062
Only now it'll make no sense.

04:13.096 --> 04:17.266
<i>"Cast of Parks and Rec Peter" away!</i>

04:21.471 --> 04:23.572
I can't believe you dragged me
to that fraud.

04:23.607 --> 04:25.608
That man has nothing to offer me.

04:27.511 --> 04:29.078
Tony Robbins.

04:29.112 --> 04:30.613
Listen, I don't have long.

04:30.647 --> 04:33.415
If I get soaked in the rain,
I'll be too heavy to move.

04:33.450 --> 04:36.085
Peter, I've seen thousands
of people over the years

04:36.119 --> 04:38.254
and helped every single one of them.

04:38.288 --> 04:41.257
I'm not going to let you
be my first failure.

04:41.291 --> 04:42.992
I told you, I don't want your help.

04:47.164 --> 04:48.764
Peter, I swear,

04:48.798 --> 04:50.766
I won't stop trying to help you
no matter what.

04:56.139 --> 04:57.773
Oh, my God! Peter, stop the car!

04:57.807 --> 04:59.942
I think he got struck by lightning.

05:02.345 --> 05:04.947
Wait, w-where is he?

05:04.981 --> 05:06.115
He's gone.

05:06.149 --> 05:08.284
This is freaking me out.

05:08.318 --> 05:11.120
Are... are you carrying a flask now?

05:11.154 --> 05:13.789
This is about you
getting better, not me.

05:19.663 --> 05:21.897
Hey, there's Hudson.

05:23.366 --> 05:25.968
Stewie, you're, like, 100 times
more advanced than that kid.

05:26.002 --> 05:27.636
Why do you want to hang out
with him so badly?

05:27.671 --> 05:29.538
He's just, like, a cool guy.

05:29.573 --> 05:32.141
Hi, Stewie.
I'm putting sand on a cat poo.

05:32.175 --> 05:33.576
Cool!

05:34.844 --> 05:36.478
I like you, Stewie.

05:36.513 --> 05:38.647
Can I come over for a playdate?

05:38.682 --> 05:40.482
Oh, my God.

05:40.517 --> 05:42.251
Oh, my God. Oh, my God.
Oh, my God. Oh, my God.

05:42.285 --> 05:43.519
Yes, yes, yes, yes, yes!

05:43.553 --> 05:45.821
Brian, can Hudson come over
for a playdate?

05:45.855 --> 05:47.823
Sure, I guess so.

05:47.857 --> 05:49.825
Never heard you ask
for a playdate before.

05:49.859 --> 05:52.161
I know, but there's a first time
for everything.

05:52.195 --> 05:54.496
Like when I finally built
the Leaning Tower of Pisa

05:54.531 --> 05:56.031
out of LEGOS.

05:58.034 --> 05:59.435
I did it!

05:59.469 --> 06:01.837
Mom! Come look! Mom!

06:01.871 --> 06:03.572
Yeah, be right there, Stewie.

06:03.607 --> 06:05.040
Where's the bush vodka?

06:06.209 --> 06:07.576
Where is it? Where is it?!

06:07.611 --> 06:09.945
Ah, there it is.

06:09.980 --> 06:12.381
Hi, Stewbie.

06:12.415 --> 06:15.217
You playing with your kitty cat?

06:21.224 --> 06:24.360
Ah, the privacy of all glass around me.

06:24.394 --> 06:26.362
Finally, I can pick my nose.

07:42.339 --> 07:44.440
Hey, Peter, next time use a tissue.

07:44.474 --> 07:47.209
- Who said that?
- It's me. Tony Robbins.

07:47.243 --> 07:48.377
Tony Robbins?

07:48.411 --> 07:49.945
That's impossible. You're dead.

07:49.979 --> 07:51.113
That may be true,

07:51.147 --> 07:52.781
but the lightning bolt that killed me

07:52.816 --> 07:55.617
seems to have magically
transferred my personal power...

07:55.652 --> 07:57.119
Trademark... into your car.

07:57.153 --> 07:59.955
Peter, I told you
I was going to help you,

07:59.989 --> 08:02.791
and I'm not leaving
until I make good on my promise.

08:02.826 --> 08:04.360
Suit yourself.

08:04.394 --> 08:06.962
Hey, if you're dead,
can you ask Bill Paxton

08:06.996 --> 08:08.697
if he's the same as Bill Pullman?

08:08.732 --> 08:11.300
Sure. Hang on.

08:11.334 --> 08:13.302
He said no, but he winked.

08:13.336 --> 08:14.978
Ah!

08:19.342 --> 08:21.510
Hey, Stewie,
let's play cops and robbers.

08:21.544 --> 08:24.146
Bang! Bang! Bang! Got you.

08:24.180 --> 08:25.914
Gun?

08:25.949 --> 08:29.685
Oh, that's-that's not...
that's not a gun.

08:32.507 --> 08:34.857
<i>These are guns.</i>

08:34.891 --> 08:36.492
You're welcome, Paul Hogan.

08:36.526 --> 08:39.194
Any time someone says
a weapon is not what it is,

08:39.229 --> 08:41.163
Paul Hogan gets a royalty.

08:41.197 --> 08:43.232
Royalty check, Mr. Hogan.

08:43.266 --> 08:45.367
Thanks, Jumpy.

08:45.402 --> 08:48.036
Whoa! What are all these for?

08:48.071 --> 08:49.171
Oh, the yoozh:

08:49.205 --> 08:50.939
destroying enemies, world domination.

08:50.974 --> 08:52.174
Oh, and killing my mother.

08:52.208 --> 08:53.942
You want to hurt your mommy?

08:53.977 --> 08:55.177
Stewie?

08:55.211 --> 08:56.678
Blast! Here she comes.

08:56.713 --> 09:00.516
Well, look at the handsome little boys.

09:00.550 --> 09:02.684
Come downstairs. I made your favorites:

09:02.719 --> 09:05.721
grilled cheese
cut to look like a dinosaur.

09:05.755 --> 09:07.890
Ugh. They never look like a dinosaur.

09:07.924 --> 09:10.526
- Your mom seems nice.
- She's a slag.

09:10.560 --> 09:12.361
Well, I hope you don't use your guns

09:12.395 --> 09:14.196
to kill your mom or do anything bad.

09:14.230 --> 09:15.364
'Cause if you do,

09:15.398 --> 09:17.032
I won't be able to play with you,

09:17.066 --> 09:18.901
and that's my favorite thing now.

09:18.935 --> 09:20.202
It is?

09:20.236 --> 09:22.070
- Uh-huh.
- Mine, too.

09:22.105 --> 09:24.873
You know what?
I'm going to let her live.

09:24.908 --> 09:27.075
I must say, I've been evil so long,

09:27.110 --> 09:28.877
I've forgotten
what it's like to be kind.

09:28.912 --> 09:31.380
And it's all because
of our friendship, Hudson.

09:31.414 --> 09:33.816
- You really mean that?
- You bet I do.

09:33.850 --> 09:35.551
And I always tell it like it is,

09:35.585 --> 09:38.187
like when I used to write tombstones.

09:40.976 --> 09:43.645
Complained a lot is what she did.

09:48.331 --> 09:50.432
Stewie, what are you doing?

09:50.467 --> 09:51.934
Having a funeral, Bri.

09:51.968 --> 09:54.236
Say good-bye to Evil Stewie.

09:54.270 --> 09:56.271
Did we get a pool?

09:58.131 --> 09:59.565
Is this a pool?

10:05.768 --> 10:07.768
Oh, my God! Oh, my God! Oh, my God!

10:07.804 --> 10:10.105
Stewie, slow down, slow down.
What happened?

10:10.140 --> 10:12.074
We went to the zoo. We saw an ape.

10:12.108 --> 10:13.409
At first we didn't think we'd see him

10:13.443 --> 10:15.177
'cause he was, like, hiding
back in his house.

10:15.211 --> 10:16.745
But then he came out. We saw him!

10:16.780 --> 10:18.747
<i>We saw the ape! He was big.</i>

10:18.782 --> 10:20.249
And then... and then... and then...

10:20.283 --> 10:21.784
And then... and then... and then...

10:21.818 --> 10:23.585
Okay, I get it. You had fun.

10:23.620 --> 10:26.561
Wait, you're not mad
I went without you, are you?

10:26.597 --> 10:28.524
No, no, I-I was only going for you.

10:28.558 --> 10:31.593
And maybe to taunt the animals
that aren't able to leave.

10:31.628 --> 10:33.128
Which is all of them.

10:33.163 --> 10:34.763
Losers.

10:34.798 --> 10:36.265
All right, you have to take us to lunch,

10:36.299 --> 10:38.634
but first we need to take our nap.

10:43.006 --> 10:46.642
Here's your triple bacon burger
and your onion rings.

10:47.811 --> 10:49.111
Ah, crap.

10:49.145 --> 10:50.712
There's only nine pieces of bacon.

10:50.747 --> 10:51.980
I paid for 12.

10:52.015 --> 10:53.449
But I don't wanna make a fuss.

10:53.483 --> 10:54.983
Peter, listen to yourself.

10:55.018 --> 10:58.120
No one will respect you until
you respect yourself first.

10:58.154 --> 10:59.721
Yeah. But I'm a nobody.

10:59.756 --> 11:01.123
You're not a nobody.

11:01.157 --> 11:03.826
Your meal is just as important
as anyone else.

11:03.860 --> 11:05.127
You're right.

11:05.161 --> 11:06.628
I'm not a nobody.

11:06.663 --> 11:07.830
Say it again.

11:07.864 --> 11:09.231
I'm not a nobody!

11:09.265 --> 11:10.732
That's the spirit, Peter.

11:10.767 --> 11:12.801
Now yell at that nobody in the window.

11:12.836 --> 11:14.970
You there! I demand more bacon.

11:15.004 --> 11:16.972
Oh, I'm sorry. Here's more bacon.

11:17.006 --> 11:18.807
That's not more bacon...

11:18.842 --> 11:20.642
This is more bacon!

11:20.677 --> 11:22.644
Big day, Mr. Hogan.

11:22.679 --> 11:24.680
Keeping coming, Jumpy!

11:26.683 --> 11:28.650
<i>Here's your Star Wars kids' meal.</i>

11:28.685 --> 11:30.352
Which action figures did we get?

11:30.386 --> 11:32.087
I got Kylo Ren.

11:32.121 --> 11:34.690
I got the role during the
two months I was a hot actor,

11:34.724 --> 11:36.325
and now they're stuck with me.

11:36.359 --> 11:37.926
I got Forest Whitaker.

11:37.961 --> 11:40.696
Even as a toy you can't tell
where he's looking.

11:40.730 --> 11:43.198
I wish I had the poorly-cast Kylo Ren.

11:44.734 --> 11:46.668
Here, Stewie. You can have mine.

11:46.703 --> 11:48.670
You're giving me the better one?

11:48.705 --> 11:50.172
Why would you do that?

11:50.206 --> 11:51.673
Because you're my friend.

11:51.708 --> 11:53.675
Yes.

11:53.710 --> 11:55.878
You're my friend.

11:55.912 --> 11:58.680
You're my best friend.

11:58.715 --> 12:02.351
Let's choke on these... together.

12:08.925 --> 12:10.692
That was fun.

12:10.727 --> 12:13.061
Let's switch.

12:22.572 --> 12:24.373
Okay, guys. Time to play "parachute."

12:24.407 --> 12:25.574
Grab an end

12:25.608 --> 12:27.709
and... lift.

12:27.744 --> 12:29.578
You know who loves "parachute"?

12:29.580 --> 12:30.979
My best friend, Hudson.

12:31.014 --> 12:32.881
- You know Hudson?
- I know Hudson, too.

12:32.916 --> 12:34.716
Are you going to his birthday
party tomorrow?

12:34.751 --> 12:36.051
I'm autistic.

12:36.085 --> 12:37.753
And... lift.

12:37.787 --> 12:38.887
Birthday party?

12:38.922 --> 12:40.622
Yeah, it's at the Family Fun Zone.

12:40.657 --> 12:41.990
Everyone was invited.

12:42.025 --> 12:44.326
I take up a great deal
of the teacher's time.

12:48.264 --> 12:50.232
- Where's the mail?
- On the table.

12:50.266 --> 12:51.934
What's going on? You seem upset.

12:51.968 --> 12:53.902
Oh, you're a... you're a real student

12:53.937 --> 12:55.270
of the human condition, aren't you?

12:55.305 --> 12:57.406
Yet, somehow, it escapes your writing.

12:57.440 --> 12:59.408
Whoa! Why are you attacking me?

12:59.442 --> 13:00.776
I'm sorry, Brian.

13:00.810 --> 13:04.079
Everyone but me got an invite
to Hudson's birthday.

13:04.113 --> 13:05.414
I know why this happened.

13:05.448 --> 13:07.916
I called him my best friend too quickly.

13:07.951 --> 13:09.451
Well, maybe it wasn't meant to be.

13:09.485 --> 13:11.453
But, hey, I'm-I'm still your friend.

13:12.956 --> 13:15.090
Yeah, but Hudson isn't.

13:15.124 --> 13:18.427
And that's just something
I have to live with.

13:32.175 --> 13:34.343
Stewie, it's 2:00 a.m.

13:34.377 --> 13:36.144
Revenge doesn't sleep.

13:36.179 --> 13:37.946
Come on. Come back to bed.

13:37.981 --> 13:39.114
No.

13:39.148 --> 13:41.283
There's something I gotta do.

13:41.317 --> 13:42.818
Go get 'em, tiger.

13:42.852 --> 13:44.553
Hey.

13:44.587 --> 13:46.555
Shut your (BLEEP) mouth.

13:55.932 --> 13:58.133
Victory shall be mine.

14:01.671 --> 14:03.505
Ha. That's what the baby used to say

14:03.539 --> 14:05.040
when I was your age.

14:05.074 --> 14:08.010
<i>Shut up, Dad.
I'm watching Rick and Morty.</i>

14:11.014 --> 14:15.317
So... does Mommy have friends
over sometimes at night?

14:15.351 --> 14:17.419
Sometimes.

14:17.453 --> 14:20.822
It must be weird having only
women come over to see Mommy.

14:20.857 --> 14:22.524
No, it's mostly men.

14:22.558 --> 14:24.259
Oh, it is.

14:24.293 --> 14:26.528
And you'd be comfortable
telling that to a judge?

14:33.605 --> 14:34.939
Good morning, family.

14:34.973 --> 14:37.374
My, who's this go-getter?

14:37.409 --> 14:39.843
Tony Robbins has helped me
become a better person.

14:39.878 --> 14:44.348
In fact, today, I'm gonna ask
for... nay, demand a raise.

14:44.382 --> 14:46.183
"Nay"? Wow.

14:46.217 --> 14:48.285
This new you is a bigger surprise

14:48.320 --> 14:49.853
than when they're making fun
of a celebrity

14:49.888 --> 14:51.388
<i>on Saturday Night Live</i>

14:51.423 --> 14:54.525
and the real-life celebrity
walks in behind them.

14:54.559 --> 14:57.728
Boy, they're really
socking it to this celebrity.

14:57.762 --> 15:00.864
Yeah, can you imagine
how mad the celebrity would be?

15:00.899 --> 15:03.033
I mean, wherever they are
at this particular moment,

15:03.068 --> 15:04.702
if they're watching, they must be...

15:05.904 --> 15:07.037
Oh.

15:07.072 --> 15:08.606
That's the actual celebrity

15:08.640 --> 15:10.140
walking up right behind 'em.

15:10.175 --> 15:12.142
He-he's catching 'em right in the act.

15:12.177 --> 15:14.044
<i>The-The SNL actor doesn't know.</i>

15:14.079 --> 15:15.546
Aw, he's gonna get in trouble.

15:15.580 --> 15:17.881
Look how mad the actual celebrity is.

15:17.916 --> 15:19.583
He's folding his arms and frowning.

15:19.618 --> 15:22.086
<i>He tapped the SNL actor on the shoulder.</i>

15:22.120 --> 15:24.722
<i>Look how surprised the SNL actor is!</i>

15:24.756 --> 15:26.724
Oh! He's completely busted!

15:26.758 --> 15:29.793
How is this happening?!

15:31.930 --> 15:33.263
Oh, my God!

15:33.298 --> 15:35.899
I can't believe it!

15:35.934 --> 15:38.402
I was watching upstairs on Hulu!

15:38.436 --> 15:40.671
I saw it on my phone!

15:40.705 --> 15:42.773
My plane has Wi-Fi!

15:47.646 --> 15:50.280
Stewie? Stewie?

15:51.816 --> 15:54.585
"Quahog Family Fun Zone"?

15:57.288 --> 15:58.455
Uh-oh.

15:59.958 --> 16:02.092
Stewie's dug up all his weapons.

16:02.127 --> 16:04.261
Oh, my God, I've got to stop him.

16:04.295 --> 16:06.463
Go get 'em, tiger.

16:06.498 --> 16:07.631
Hey.

16:07.666 --> 16:09.900
Shut your (BLEEP) mouth.

16:13.638 --> 16:15.272
Tony! You're not gonna believe it.

16:15.306 --> 16:17.441
I demanded a raise
just like you told me to

16:17.475 --> 16:18.942
and they gave it to me.

16:18.977 --> 16:20.075
Tony?

16:20.111 --> 16:21.779
Tony? You in there?

16:21.813 --> 16:23.147
Guess who, Peter.

16:23.181 --> 16:24.381
Geena Davis?

16:24.416 --> 16:26.283
No, it's me, Peter. Turn around.

16:26.317 --> 16:28.819
Tony? You're alive?

16:28.853 --> 16:30.287
But... how?

16:30.321 --> 16:32.122
I saw you get struck by lightning.

16:32.157 --> 16:34.024
I was created by lightning, Peter,

16:34.059 --> 16:35.726
in a lab, like Frankenstein.

16:35.760 --> 16:37.294
And what do you think about fire?

16:38.997 --> 16:40.731
Anyway, after the lightning strike,

16:40.765 --> 16:42.232
I climbed into your trunk

16:42.267 --> 16:44.034
and that's where I've been
living the past week.

16:44.069 --> 16:47.504
So, whenever I heard your voice,
that was just you in the trunk?

16:47.539 --> 16:48.806
That's right.

16:48.840 --> 16:50.307
Why would you go to all that trouble?

16:50.341 --> 16:51.909
Peter, I told you,

16:51.943 --> 16:55.012
I wasn't going to let you be
my first failure.

16:55.046 --> 16:59.316
Wow, Tony, I don't know how
I can possibly thank you.

16:59.350 --> 17:00.984
You don't need to thank me, Peter.

17:01.019 --> 17:03.153
I have hundreds of millions of dollars.

17:03.188 --> 17:04.655
I keep it in my forehead.

17:04.689 --> 17:06.156
Well, I better be going.

17:06.191 --> 17:08.325
You have a Smart car?

17:08.359 --> 17:09.960
I have two.

17:14.065 --> 17:17.534
I'm coming, broken people!

17:23.541 --> 17:24.842
Hey, everybody,

17:24.876 --> 17:26.510
we want to give a special shout-out

17:26.544 --> 17:28.679
to little Hudson on his birthday.

17:41.893 --> 17:43.527
Oh, no. Soda!

17:43.561 --> 17:44.862
Sticky balls!

18:11.923 --> 18:13.757
Damn you all.

18:34.779 --> 18:35.913
Stewie?

18:35.947 --> 18:37.915
That's my name, don't wear it out.

18:37.949 --> 18:39.917
Yeah, let that wash over you.

18:39.951 --> 18:41.952
Learned that from a third grader.

18:41.986 --> 18:43.086
Any last words?

18:43.121 --> 18:44.121
Yeah.

18:44.155 --> 18:45.589
I'm glad to see you.

18:45.623 --> 18:48.258
You never RSVP to the invite
my mom sent.

18:48.293 --> 18:51.094
You... You invited me?

18:51.129 --> 18:53.096
Yes. He did.

18:53.131 --> 18:55.299
Brian? What are you doing here?

18:55.333 --> 18:56.767
And how do you know I was invited?

18:56.801 --> 18:58.268
Because...

18:58.303 --> 19:00.103
I threw your invitation away.

19:00.138 --> 19:01.438
You what?

19:01.472 --> 19:02.773
I know. I'm sorry.

19:02.807 --> 19:05.609
I-I just... I saw how you were
connecting with Hudson

19:05.643 --> 19:08.312
and I-I was afraid
of losing our friendship.

19:08.346 --> 19:09.813
Friendship?

19:09.848 --> 19:12.115
Brian, you and I
have never been friends.

19:12.150 --> 19:13.951
We... We haven't?

19:13.985 --> 19:15.619
No. Friends are people

19:15.653 --> 19:17.221
who come in and out of our lives.

19:17.255 --> 19:19.289
But you and I are family.

19:19.324 --> 19:20.657
That's forever.

19:27.498 --> 19:29.466
Sorry I caused all this trouble.

19:29.500 --> 19:31.034
I hope you can forgive me.

19:31.069 --> 19:34.071
Ah, that's okay, nothing could
ever come between us.

19:34.105 --> 19:36.840
I'm even going to
make a speech at your wedding.

19:36.875 --> 19:38.976
So Brian and I are down in Mexico,

19:39.010 --> 19:41.311
and, as usual, he doesn't have
any cash on him.

19:41.346 --> 19:42.713
That's probably why your parents

19:42.747 --> 19:44.514
are paying for all this, right, Evan?

19:44.549 --> 19:46.149
<i>Wait, hold on. Evan?</i>

19:46.184 --> 19:47.417
<i>Why am I gay in this?</i>

19:47.452 --> 19:48.752
<i>Ah, it's the end of the show.</i>

19:48.786 --> 19:50.254
<i>We sometimes do something silly here.</i>

19:56.367 --> 19:58.902
So, now that you got me back
as a friend,

19:58.937 --> 20:01.738
what are all the great things
you have planned for us?

20:01.773 --> 20:04.641
Uh... we could... go see a movie.

20:04.676 --> 20:07.411
Oh, a movie. That's a great idea.

20:07.445 --> 20:08.912
You know what'll get me out
of this funk?

20:08.947 --> 20:10.581
<i>The Equalizer 2.</i>

20:10.615 --> 20:12.482
Okay. All right, fine.

20:12.517 --> 20:13.650
I got... I got nothing.

20:13.685 --> 20:14.918
Exactly.

20:14.953 --> 20:16.253
And you were such a jealous little bitch

20:16.287 --> 20:18.956
that you had to ruin the one
friendship I really cared about.

20:18.990 --> 20:21.124
You're just a big jerk and I hate you,

20:21.159 --> 20:23.260
and there's nothing you can do
to make up for it.

20:23.294 --> 20:24.528
Fine.

20:24.562 --> 20:26.430
Maybe I'll just go out
and get some ice cream.

20:26.464 --> 20:27.831
Ice cream?

20:27.866 --> 20:29.099
I like ice cream.

20:29.133 --> 20:32.035
Yeah, I don't know.
I think it's more of a bigger kid thing.

20:32.070 --> 20:34.438
No, no, no! No. I've had
ice cream, like, six times.

20:34.472 --> 20:36.073
All right, come on, let's go.

20:37.809 --> 20:39.943
You know, Brian, I'm starting to think

20:39.978 --> 20:42.946
we're going to get through
our... Rocky Road.

20:48.152 --> 20:49.786
We had a lot of laughs tonight,

20:49.821 --> 20:51.622
but let's remember the important thing:

20:51.656 --> 20:53.790
you can't put a price on your happiness,

20:53.825 --> 20:56.293
which is why I have: it's $6,000.

20:56.327 --> 20:59.229
See you in Fort Myers, probably.

20:59.264 --> 21:02.780
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.tv